<%- include('partials/head.ejs') %> 
<div id="content">
  <div class="inner">
  <article class="box post post-excerpt">
    <h2>About this Project</h2>
    <p>
      Ever done the
      <a target="_blank" href="https://100daysofcode.com"
        >100daysofcode.com</a
      >
      challenge and found yourself skipping, forgetting which day you were on, etc?
    </p>
    <p>
      This project aims to help you stay consistent by giving you friendly reminders, a simple
      way to keep track of what day you are on, and will allow you to tweet
      directly from it (hopefully!).
    </p>
    <p>
      OS_100Days is an opensource project from
      <a target="_blank" href="https://codingwithdrew.com/">Coding With Drew</a>, built by a
      community of aspiring software engineers who are learning about collaboration on GitHub.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article class="box post post-excerpt">
    <h2>How to use it</h2>
    <p>The project is still under development. Today you can:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/signup">Sign up</a> with a username, an email address and a password.</li>
      <li><a href="/signin">Log in</a> with your username and password.</li>
      <li>See the home page, where your challenge details (username, current challenge, challenge
        duration and number of repos worked on) will be shown.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Accounts are not kept for now: the database is reset every time the app restarts, so you may need to sign up again.</p>
    <p>
      Reminders, day tracking and tweeting from the app are the goals of the project and are not
      available yet. Have questions? See the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article class="box post post-excerpt">
    <h2>Get involved</h2>
    <p>
      The code is open, and everyone is welcome to help. If you know HTML, CSS or JavaScript, this
      project is for you. Join Drew Karriker and friends on
      <a target="_blank" href="https://discord.gg/AntJA73Qx2">Discord</a> (the #OS_100Days
      channel), or look for an issue to work on on
      <a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/drewlearns/OS_100days/issues">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
</div>

